{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "b6f4f6d2-8f2a-4a3a-9c1e-2b7a8f1e9c3d",
    "name": "RATA Healthcare Scheduling System",
    "description": "Auth Service (:3001) and Schedule Service (:3002) GraphQL APIs for the Healthcare Scheduling System.\n\nFolders are meant to be run top to bottom, either one request at a time or via \"Run collection\" (Collection Runner / Newman) — each step saves what the next step needs into collection variables, and a fresh random email is generated for Register/Create Customer so the whole collection can be re-run repeatedly against the same database:\n\n1. Auth Service — Register, then Login (saves `accessToken`), then Validate Token.\n2. Schedule Service - Customer — Create (saves `customerId`), Update, List, Get.\n3. Schedule Service - Doctor — Create (saves `doctorId`), Update, List, Get.\n4. Schedule Service - Schedule — Create (saves `scheduleId`), List (with filters), Get.\n5. Error Cases — missing/invalid auth, duplicate email, invalid customer/doctor id, and a doctor double-booked at the same time as the schedule created in step 4 (must run before Cleanup deletes it).\n6. Cleanup — deletes the schedule, then the customer, then the doctor (FK-safe order).\n\nAll requests use Postman's native GraphQL body mode, so the query and variables are editable directly in the Postman UI.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "authServiceUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:3001/graphql",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "scheduleServiceUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:3002/graphql",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "userEmail",
      "value": "doctor.admin@clinic.com",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "userPassword",
      "value": "supersecret",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "accessToken",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "customerId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "customerEmail",
      "value": "john.doe@example.com",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "doctorId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "scheduleId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
